/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (A list is suitable because readings are ordered by day, supports indexing and slicing, and grows dynamically. append is O\(1\) amortised; insert at an arbitrary position is O\(n\) because later elements shift; pop\(\) at the end is O\(1\), while pop\(i\) is O\(n\); sort is O\(n log n\).)
/E (A list is suitable because readings are ordered by day, supports indexing and slicing, and grows dynamically. append is O\(1\) amortised; insert at an arbitrary position is O\(n\) because later elements shift; pop\(\) at the end is O\(1\), while pop\(i\) is O\(n\); sort is O\(n log n\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
