/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (Inserting a late reading at its date in a Python list costs O\(n\) due to shifting. A list remains suitable for a small or moderate yearly dataset and simple sequential reports. For frequent insertions at both ends, deque is useful; for date-keyed random access or missing dates, a dictionary may be appropriate.)
/E (Inserting a late reading at its date in a Python list costs O\(n\) due to shifting. A list remains suitable for a small or moderate yearly dataset and simple sequential reports. For frequent insertions at both ends, deque is useful; for date-keyed random access or missing dates, a dictionary may be appropriate.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 49 0 R
/T (A deque\(maxlen=7\) can maintain a rolling seven-day window; update a running sum as old readings leave and new ones enter. This is O\(n\) total time and O\(7\)=O\(1\) window space. A full date dictionary provides average O\(1\) lookup by date but needs O\(n\) storage)
/E (A deque\(maxlen=7\) can maintain a rolling seven-day window; update a running sum as old readings leave and new ones enter. This is O\(n\) total time and O\(7\)=O\(1\) window space. A full date dictionary provides average O\(1\) lookup by date but needs O\(n\) storage)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
