627 0 obj
<<
/Title (A flat list of \(train, station, arrival, departure, days\) tuples scanned for each query costs O\(S\) per query. A station index costs O\(k\) to inspect the k trains at that station \(plus sorting O\(k log k\) if ordered output is needed\). The nested timetable and index use O\(S\) total storage; the index adds O\(S\) references/entries. A flat list is simpler but slower for repeated station queries.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 557 0 R
>>
endobj
628 0 obj
<<
/Title (For the small hand-check: the two Ravi records normalise to 9840012345 and merge into one group with two name spellings and two email addresses. The two Meena records normalise to 9876543210 and merge. The record with no phone is skipped by this identity rule and should be reviewed separately rather than guessed.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 561 0 R
>>
