/Title (Both list comprehension and generator expression take O\(n\) time to examine n readings. The list stores O\(n\) results; the generator stores O\(1\) iterator state \(excluding data retained elsewhere\). A list comprehension is not always best: use it when the result is needed repeatedly or indexed; use a generator for one-pass processing and lower memory use.)
